{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR DECISION REFINED 2026-08-12: 4-digit (single-quad) short IDs are DEPRECATED as a reference form — escalating collisions make them a pain point. Do NOT break existing 4-digit usage (compatibility resolution stays), but stop advertising them: docs and agent guidance should name the preferred forms — alias (preferred), 8-digit (two-quad) prefix, full canonical id, Jira/bridge ids. For THIS bug's fix: the enrichment-drain prose scanner must stop treating bare 4-hex fragments as ticket prefixes (the collision class measured here) — use the existing quiet-resolution seam; commit-subject and explicit-reference resolution keep today's behavior. Also sweep docs/agent guidance (AGENTS.md, docs/*) to stop advertising 4-digit references."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786503211377071001,"uuid":"029ac469-ecf7-4356-99c4-5ddee4648470"}